WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.425
Scripts are training wheels.

00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:03.919
Customize them so they sound like you.

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.125
This lesson is about dm scripts that start conversations.

00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:08.194
Training wheels scripts.

00:00:08.194 --> 00:00:10.688
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.688 --> 00:00:14.250
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:19.594
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.594 --> 00:00:23.513
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.513 --> 00:00:27.432
Stay practical: customize one script before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:32.156
The goal is a conversation, not a hard pitch in message one.

00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:34.359
Remember the objective: customize one script.

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:38.396
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.396 --> 00:00:42.801
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.838
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:51.243
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.243 --> 00:00:53.812
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:53.812 --> 00:00:55.280
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.074
Customize one script with their context, your one-liner, and a soft ask.

